clipmanx (0.1.5) unstable; urgency=low

  * Added image clipboard support: copied images are stored in history,
    shown with a thumbnail and hover preview, and can be copied back.
  * Large images are scaled down to at most 2048px on the longest side.
  * Existing history files from earlier versions are still loaded.

 -- Victor Sejas <vrsejas@gmail.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 08:23:25 -0400

clipmanx (0.1.4) unstable; urgency=low

  * Tray icon now follows the desktop dark/light theme live, using the XDG
    desktop portal color-scheme with a GTK settings fallback.
  * Tray icon is swapped in place instead of being recreated on theme change.
  * Renamed the "Auto Detect" icon theme option to "System".

 -- Victor Sejas <vrsejas@gmail.com>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:54:55 -0400

clipmanx (0.1.3) unstable; urgency=low

  * Switched to native Debian source format so the package version matches the
    git tag exactly (output is now clipmanx_0.1.3_all.deb, no -1 suffix)
  * Standardised install path: download the .deb from GitHub Releases and run
    apt-get install. The legacy install-latest.sh one-liner is no longer
    documented.
  * Cleaned up README and dropped the "early development" notice.

 -- Victor Sejas <vrsejas@gmail.com>  Wed, 03 Jun 2026 23:12:40 -0400

clipmanx (0.1.2) unstable; urgency=low

  * Fixed hover preview occupying the full screen and covering the list when
    the clipboard entry was very tall (compute size from the larger free side
    of the main window and move() before show_all so it appears in place)
  * Fixed text selections leaking into the system CLIPBOARD: the re-claim on
    owner close is now scoped to CLIPBOARD events and tracks the last CLIPBOARD
    text separately from cross-source dedup state

 -- Victor Sejas <vrsejas@gmail.com>  Wed, 03 Jun 2026 22:49:37 -0400

clipmanx (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Unified left- and right-click tray behaviour into a single full-view popup
  * Scrollable hover preview with 800 ms delay and Pango-measured height
  * Disabled PRIMARY-selection capture by default
  * Skip clipboard captures whose source window is a terminal emulator
  * Fixed startup deadlock by forking before importing GTK
  * Added tooltip-delay setting and renamed debug logging module to logger
  * Added unit tests for history, settings, and terminal-window detection

 -- Victor Sejas <vrsejas@gmail.com>  Wed, 03 Jun 2026 22:16:22 -0400

